---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="How Conclave AX works" description="Understand the Conclave AX Cloud, Host, Worker, and Account model.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
    <h1>One path from request to result.</h1>
    <p class="section-intro">Conclave AX separates coordination from local capability, so your execution path stays understandable as work gets more complex.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card"><h3>1. Conclave AX</h3><p>Ask questions, start work, review progress, and inspect the result in the authenticated app.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>2. Conclave Cloud</h3><p>Cloud authenticates people, enforces Workspace permissions, and coordinates the execution.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>3. Host and Worker</h3><p>Your Host provides a machine. A Worker provides the AI or tool capability for one assignment.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button-primary" href="https://app.conclaveax.com">Open Conclave AX</a></div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
